    "summary": "Fiery '70 set with stellar Easy Wind and rare Frozen Logger",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a tight Working Man’s Dead/American Beauty set highlighted by an inspired Easy Wind and the rare Frozen Logger. Jerry's scorching guitar shines on Beat It On Down The Line while Bob Weir adds solid vocals on Easy Wind. Recording quality is generally excellent, making this one of the stronger late‑1970 performances.",
    "review": "The December 26, 1970 concert at Legion Stadium captures the Dead in a tight Working Man’s Dead/American Beauty phase. From the opening \"Cold Rain And Snow\" through a powerhouse first set packed with \"Easy Wind,\" \"New Minglewood Blues,\" and a scorching \"Beat It On Down The Line,\" the band is locked in. Jerry’s Gibson SG blazes, especially on \"Beat It…\" and \"Truckin',\" while Bob Weir shines on \"Easy Wind\" and \"Friend Of The Devil.\" The second set delivers the rare acoustic \"Frozen Logger,\" a soulful \"Good Lovin'\" jam (despite a splice), and closes with an uplifting \"Uncle John's Band.\" Recording quality is generally pristine, with three excellent soundboard sources; the Ashley‑Field tape is the cleanest, offering crisp separation and minimal glitches.",
